</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwBbI" aria-labelledby="Foreign_relations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Foreign_relations">Foreign relations</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt618" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBbM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Foreign relations of Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt619" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt618" id="mwBbQ">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Japan" title="Foreign relations of Japan">Foreign relations of Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBbU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen,_President_of_the_European_Commission,_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBbY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen,_President_of_the_European_Commission,_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen%2C_President_of_the_European_Commission%2C_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg/250px-Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen%2C_President_of_the_European_Commission%2C_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen%2C_President_of_the_European_Commission%2C_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg/500px-Participation_of_Ursula_von_der_Leyen%2C_President_of_the_European_Commission%2C_to_the_G7_Summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5856" data-file-height="3896" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1" id="mwBbc"/></a><figcaption id="mwBbg">Japan is a member of both the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G7" title="G7" id="mwBbk">G7</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G20" title="G20" id="mwBbo">G20</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBbs">A member state of the United Nations since 1956, Japan is one of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G4_nations" title="G4 nations" id="mwBbw">G4 countries</a> seeking reform of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Security_Council" title="Security Council" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBb0">Security Council</a>.<sup about="#mwt622" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwBb4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBb8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcA">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcE">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan is a member of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G7" title="G7" id="mwBcI">G7</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APEC" title="APEC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBcM">APEC</a>, and "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASEAN_Free_Trade_Area#ASEAN_Plus_Three" title="ASEAN Free Trade Area" id="mwBcQ">ASEAN Plus Three</a>", and is a participant in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Asia_Summit" title="East Asia Summit" id="mwBcU">East Asia Summit</a>.<sup about="#mwt625" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-terada_127-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"terada"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-terada-127"}}'><a href="#cite_note-terada-127" id="mwBcY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcg">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBck">]</span></span></a></sup> It is the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_development_aid_sovereign_state_donors" title="List of development aid sovereign state donors" id="mwBco">fifth-largest donor</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Official_Development_Assistance_(Japan)" title="Official Development Assistance (Japan)" id="mwBcs">official development assistance</a>, donating US$9.2<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBcw"> </span>billion in 2014.<sup about="#mwt628" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"}}'><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwBc0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBc4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc8">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdA">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2024, Japan had the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_diplomatic_missions" title="List of countries by number of diplomatic missions" id="mwBdE">fourth-largest diplomatic network</a> in the world.<sup about="#mwt631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-129" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-129"}}'><a href="#cite_note-129" id="mwBdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdQ">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdU">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan is widely considered to be a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_power" title="Great power" id="mwBdY">great power</a> due to its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economic_power" title="Economic power" id="mwBdc">economic power</a> and political, cultural, and military influence.<sup about="#mwt634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Milena_Steriob_130-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Milena Steriob"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Milena_Steriob-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Milena_Steriob-130" id="mwBdg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdo">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBds">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PaulWirtz2004_131-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"PaulWirtz2004"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-PaulWirtz2004-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-PaulWirtz2004-131" id="mwBdw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBd0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd4">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBeA">Japan has close economic and military <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan–United_States_relations" title="Japan–United States relations" id="mwBeE">relations with the United States</a>, with which it maintains <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Mutual_Cooperation_and_Security_between_the_United_States_and_Japan" title="Treaty of Mutual Cooperation and Security between the United States and Japan" id="mwBeI">a security alliance</a>.<sup about="#mwt640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-us-relations_132-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"us-relations"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-us-relations-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-us-relations-132" id="mwBeM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeU">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeY">]</span></span></a></sup> The United States is a major market for Japanese exports and a major source of Japanese imports, and is committed to defending the country, with military bases in Japan.<sup about="#mwt641" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-us-relations_132-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"us-relations"}}'><a href="#cite_note-us-relations-132" id="mwBec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBek">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeo">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2016, Japan announced the Free and Open Indo-Pacific vision, which frames its regional policies.<sup about="#mwt644" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwBes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe0">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt647" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwBe8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfE">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfI">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan is also a member of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quadrilateral_Security_Dialogue" title="Quadrilateral Security Dialogue" id="mwBfM">Quadrilateral Security Dialogue</a> ("the Quad"), a multilateral security dialogue reformed in 2017 aiming to limit Chinese influence in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-Pacific" title="Indo-Pacific" id="mwBfQ">Indo-Pacific</a> region, along with the United States, Australia, and India.<sup about="#mwt650" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135"}}'><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwBfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfc">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt653" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-136" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136"}}'><a href="#cite_note-136" id="mwBfk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfs">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBf0">Japan is engaged in several territorial disputes with its neighbors. It contests Russia's control of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuril_Islands_dispute" title="Kuril Islands dispute" id="mwBf4">Southern Kuril Islands</a>, which were occupied by the Soviet Union in 1945.<sup about="#mwt656" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwBf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgE">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgI">]</span></span></a></sup> South Korea's control of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liancourt_Rocks" title="Liancourt Rocks" id="mwBgM">Liancourt Rocks</a> is acknowledged but not accepted as they are claimed by Japan.<sup about="#mwt659" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-takeshima_138-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"takeshima"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-takeshima-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-takeshima-138" id="mwBgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgY">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgc">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's relations with China are marked by both deep economic ties as well as tensions over Taiwan, security, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senkaku_Islands" title="Senkaku Islands" id="mwBgg">Senkaku Islands</a>.<sup about="#mwt662" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwBgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgs">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt665" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-140" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-140" id="mwBg0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBg4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBg8">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwBhE" aria-labelledby="Military"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Military">Military</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt666" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBhI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Japan Self-Defense Forces"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt667" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt666" id="mwBhM">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Self-Defense_Forces" title="Japan Self-Defense Forces">Japan Self-Defense Forces</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBhQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_Navy_051115-N-8492C-125_The_Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force_(JMSDF)_destroyer_JDS_Kongou_(DDG_173)_sails_in_formation_with_other_JMSDF_ships_and_ships_assigned_to_the_USS_Kitty_Hawk_Carrier_Strike_Group.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBhU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_Navy_051115-N-8492C-125_The_Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force_(JMSDF)_destroyer_JDS_Kongou_(DDG_173)_sails_in_formation_with_other_JMSDF_ships_and_ships_assigned_to_the_USS_Kitty_Hawk_Carrier_Strike_Group.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/US_Navy_051115-N-8492C-125_The_Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force_%28JMSDF%29_destroyer_JDS_Kongou_%28DDG_173%29_sails_in_formation_with_other_JMSDF_ships_and_ships_assigned_to_the_USS_Kitty_Hawk_Carrier_Strike_Group.jpg/250px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/US_Navy_051115-N-8492C-125_The_Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force_%28JMSDF%29_destroyer_JDS_Kongou_%28DDG_173%29_sails_in_formation_with_other_JMSDF_ships_and_ships_assigned_to_the_USS_Kitty_Hawk_Carrier_Strike_Group.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3008" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBhY"/></a><figcaption id="mwBhc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kongō-class_destroyer" title="Kongō-class destroyer" id="mwBhg"><span title="Japanese-language romanization" about="#mwt668" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBhk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ja"},"2":{"wt":"Kongō"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="ja-Latn">Kongō</i></span>-class destroyer</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force" title="Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force" id="mwBho">Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBhs">Japan is the second highest-ranked Asian country in the 2025 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Peace_Index" title="Global Peace Index" id="mwBhw">Global Peace Index</a>.<sup about="#mwt671" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-141" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-141" id="mwBh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh8">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiA">]</span></span></a></sup> It spent 1.4% of its total GDP on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_budget_of_Japan" title="Military budget of Japan" id="mwBiE">its defense budget</a> and maintained the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_military_expenditures" title="List of countries by military expenditures" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBiI">tenth-largest military budget</a> in the world in 2025.<sup about="#mwt674" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SIPRI-20202_142-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"SIPRI-20202"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-SIPRI-20202-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-SIPRI-20202-142" id="mwBiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiU">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiY">]</span></span></a></sup> The country's military, the Japan Self-Defense Forces (JSDF), is restricted by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Article_9_of_the_Japanese_Constitution" title="Article 9 of the Japanese Constitution" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBic">Article 9 of the Japanese Constitution</a>, which renounces Japan's right to declare war or use military force in international disputes.<sup about="#mwt677" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143"}}'><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwBig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBik"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBio">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBis">]</span></span></a></sup> The military is governed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Defense_(Japan)" title="Ministry of Defense (Japan)" id="mwBiw">Ministry of Defense</a>, and primarily consists of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Ground_Self-Defense_Force" title="Japan Ground Self-Defense Force" id="mwBi0">Japan Ground Self-Defense Force</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Maritime_Self-Defense_Force" title="Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force" id="mwBi4">Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Air_Self-Defense_Force" title="Japan Air Self-Defense Force" id="mwBi8">Japan Air Self-Defense Force</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Iraq_Reconstruction_and_Support_Group" title="Japanese Iraq Reconstruction and Support Group" id="mwBjA">deployment of troops to Iraq</a> and Afghanistan marked the first overseas use of Japan's military since World War II.<sup about="#mwt680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-144" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-144"}}'><a href="#cite_note-144" id="mwBjE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjM">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBjU">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Japan" title="Government of Japan" id="mwBjY">Government of Japan</a> has been making changes to its security policy which include the establishment of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Security_Council_(Japan)" title="National Security Council (Japan)" id="mwBjc">National Security Council</a>, the adoption of the National Security Strategy, and the development of the National Defense Program Guidelines.<sup about="#mwt683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Japan's_Security_Policy_145-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Japan&apos;s Security Policy"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Japan&apos;s_Security_Policy-145"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Japan's_Security_Policy-145" id="mwBjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjo">[</span>144<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjs">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2015, the Japanese parliament passed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legislation_for_Peace_and_Security" title="Legislation for Peace and Security" id="mwBjw">Legislation for Peace and Security</a>, allowing the JSDF to participate in foreign conflicts in an "existential crisis situation".<sup about="#mwt686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kuro2_146-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"kuro2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-kuro2-146"}}'><a href="#cite_note-kuro2-146" id="mwBj0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBj4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBj8">[</span>145<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkA">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2022, Prime Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fumio_Kishida" title="Fumio Kishida" id="mwBkE">Fumio Kishida</a> instructed the government to increase spending by 65% until 2027.<sup about="#mwt689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-147" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147"}}'><a href="#cite_note-147" id="mwBkI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkQ">[</span>146<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkU">]</span></span></a></sup> Recent tensions, particularly with North Korea and China, have reignited the debate over the status of the JSDF and its relation to Japanese society.<sup about="#mwt692" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-148" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-148"}}'><a href="#cite_note-148" id="mwBkY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkg">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt695" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-149" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-149"}}'><a href="#cite_note-149" id="mwBko"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBks"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkw">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBk0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwBk4" aria-labelledby="Law_enforcement"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Law_enforcement">Law enforcement</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt696" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBk8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Law enforcement in Japan"},"2":{"wt":"Law of Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt697" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt696" id="mwBlA">Main articles: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_enforcement_in_Japan" title="Law enforcement in Japan">Law enforcement in Japan</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_of_Japan" title="Law of Japan">Law of Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBlE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:警視庁_-_panoramio.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBlI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:警視庁_-_panoramio.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%E8%AD%A6%E8%A6%96%E5%BA%81_-_panoramio.jpg/250px-%E8%AD%A6%E8%A6%96%E5%BA%81_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%E8%AD%A6%E8%A6%96%E5%BA%81_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-%E8%AD%A6%E8%A6%96%E5%BA%81_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5184" data-file-height="3456" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBlM"/></a><figcaption id="mwBlQ">The headquarters of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Metropolitan_Police_Department" title="Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department" id="mwBlU">Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBlY">Domestic security in Japan is provided mainly by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prefectural_police_department" title="Prefectural police department" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBlc">prefectural police departments</a>, under the oversight of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Police_Agency_(Japan)" title="National Police Agency (Japan)" id="mwBlg">National Police Agency</a>.<sup about="#mwt700" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-150" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150"}}'><a href="#cite_note-150" id="mwBlk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBls">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlw">]</span></span></a></sup> As the central coordinating body for the Prefectural Police Departments, the National Police Agency is administered by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Public_Safety_Commission_(Japan)" title="National Public Safety Commission (Japan)" id="mwBl0">National Public Safety Commission</a>.<sup about="#mwt703" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NPA1977-2_151-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NPA1977-2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NPA1977-2-151"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NPA1977-2-151" id="mwBl4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBl8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmA">[</span>150<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmE">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_Assault_Team" title="Special Assault Team" id="mwBmI">Special Assault Team</a> comprises national-level <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Counter-terrorism" title="Counter-terrorism" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBmM">counter-terrorism</a> tactical units that cooperate with territorial-level <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riot_Police_Unit#Specialist_squads" title="Riot Police Unit" id="mwBmQ">Anti-Firearms Squads and Counter-NBC Terrorism Squads</a>.<sup about="#mwt706" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WP_152-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WP"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WP-152"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WP-152" id="mwBmU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmc">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmg">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Coast_Guard" title="Japan Coast Guard" id="mwBmk">Japan Coast Guard</a> guards territorial waters surrounding Japan and uses surveillance and control countermeasures against smuggling, marine <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_crime" title="Environmental crime" id="mwBmo">environmental crime</a>, poaching, piracy, spy ships, unauthorized foreign fishing vessels, and illegal immigration.<sup about="#mwt709" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153"}}'><a href="#cite_note-153" id="mwBms"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm0">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBm8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firearm_and_Sword_Possession_Control_Law" title="Firearm and Sword Possession Control Law" id="mwBnA">Firearm and Sword Possession Control Law</a> strictly regulates the civilian ownership of guns, swords, and other weaponry.<sup about="#mwt713" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-154" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154"}}'><a href="#cite_note-154" id="mwBnE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnM">[</span>153<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt716" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-155" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-155"}}'><a href="#cite_note-155" id="mwBnU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnc">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBng">]</span></span></a></sup> According to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Office_on_Drugs_and_Crime" title="United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime" id="mwBnk">United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime</a>, among the member states of the UN that report statistics <span about="#mwt710" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBno" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt710"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt710"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2018" about="#mwt710"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt710" id="mwBns"/>, the incidence rates of violent crimes such as murder, abduction, sexual violence, and robbery are very low in Japan.<sup about="#mwt719" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-156" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-156"}}'><a href="#cite_note-156" id="mwBnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBn0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn4">[</span>155<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt722" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-157" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-157"}}'><a href="#cite_note-157" id="mwBoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoI">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt725" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-158" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-158"}}'><a href="#cite_note-158" id="mwBoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoY">[</span>157<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt728" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-159" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-159"}}'><a href="#cite_note-159" id="mwBog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBok"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoo">[</span>158<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBos">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwBow" aria-labelledby="Human_rights"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Human_rights">Human rights</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt729" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBo0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Human rights in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt730" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt729" id="mwBo4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_rights_in_Japan" title="Human rights in Japan">Human rights in Japan</a></div>

<p id="mwBo8">Japanese society traditionally places a strong emphasis on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wa_(Japanese_culture)" title="Wa (Japanese culture)" id="mwBpA">collective harmony</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collectivism" title="Collectivism" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBpE">conformity</a>, which has led to the suppression of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Individual_rights" title="Individual rights" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBpI">individual rights</a>.<sup about="#mwt733" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-h191_160-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"h191"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-h191-160"}}'><a href="#cite_note-h191-160" id="mwBpM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpU">[</span>159<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpY">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Japan" title="Constitution of Japan" id="mwBpc">Japan's constitution</a> prohibits racial and religious discrimination,<sup about="#mwt736" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-161" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161"}}'><a href="#cite_note-161" id="mwBpg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpo">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBps">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt739" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-162" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162"}}'><a href="#cite_note-162" id="mwBpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBp0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp4">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp8">]</span></span></a></sup> and the country is a signatory to numerous international human rights treaties.<sup about="#mwt742" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-q456_163-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"q456"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-q456-163"}}'><a href="#cite_note-q456-163" id="mwBqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqI">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqM">]</span></span></a></sup> However, it lacks any laws against discrimination based on race, ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, or gender identity and does not have a national human rights institution.<sup about="#mwt745" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-p620_164-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"p620"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-p620-164"}}'><a href="#cite_note-p620-164" id="mwBqQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqY">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBqg">Japan has faced criticism for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_inequality_in_Japan" title="Gender inequality in Japan" id="mwBqk">its gender inequality</a>,<sup about="#mwt748" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-p015_165-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"p015"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-p015-165"}}'><a href="#cite_note-p015-165" id="mwBqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqw">[</span>164<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq0">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same-sex_marriage_in_Japan" title="Same-sex marriage in Japan" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBq4">not allowing same-sex marriages</a>,<sup about="#mwt751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-h253_166-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"h253"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-h253-166"}}'><a href="#cite_note-h253-166" id="mwBq8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrE">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrI">]</span></span></a></sup> use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racial_profiling" title="Racial profiling" id="mwBrM">racial profiling</a> by police,<sup about="#mwt754" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-167" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-167"}}'><a href="#cite_note-167" id="mwBrQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrY">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt757" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-168" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168"}}'><a href="#cite_note-168" id="mwBrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBro">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrs">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment_in_Japan" title="Capital punishment in Japan" id="mwBrw">allowing capital punishment</a>.<sup about="#mwt760" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-169" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-169"}}'><a href="#cite_note-169" id="mwBr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr8">[</span>168<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsA">]</span></span></a></sup> Other human rights issues include the treatment of marginalized groups, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racism_in_Japan" title="Racism in Japan" id="mwBsE">ethnic minorities</a>,<sup about="#mwt763" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-r037_170-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"r037"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-r037-170"}}'><a href="#cite_note-r037-170" id="mwBsI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsQ">[</span>169<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsU">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immigration_to_Japan#Refugees_and_asylum_seekers" title="Immigration to Japan" id="mwBsY">refugees and asylum seekers</a>.<sup about="#mwt766" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-v702_171-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"v702"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-v702-171"}}'><a href="#cite_note-v702-171" id="mwBsc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsk">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBso">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwBss" aria-labelledby="Economy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Economy">Economy</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt767" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBsw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Economy of Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt768" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt767" id="mwBs0">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy_of_Japan" title="Economy of Japan">Economy of Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBs4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBs8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg/250px-Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg/500px-Nakanoshima_Skyscrapers_in_201504_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3840" data-file-height="2400" data-file-type="bitmap" height="156" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBtA"/></a><figcaption id="mwBtE">Skyscrapers in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nakanoshima" title="Nakanoshima" id="mwBtI">Nakanoshima</a>, Osaka; a major <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center" title="Financial center" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBtM">financial center</a> in Japan</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBtQ">Japan has the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(nominal)" title="List of countries by GDP (nominal)" id="mwBtU">fourth-largest economy by nominal GDP</a>, after that of the United States, China and Germany; and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(PPP)" title="List of countries by GDP (PPP)" id="mwBtY">fifth-largest by PPP-adjusted GDP</a>.<sup about="#mwt774" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-172" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-172" id="mwBtc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtk">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBto">]</span></span></a></sup> <span about="#mwt769" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBts" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2023"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2023</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt769"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt769"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2023" about="#mwt769"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt769" id="mwBtw"/>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labor_market_of_Japan" title="Labor market of Japan" id="mwBt0">Japan's labor force</a> is the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_labour_force" title="List of countries by labour force" id="mwBt4">tenth-largest</a>, consisting of over 69.2<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBt8"> </span>million workers.<sup about="#mwt775" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwBuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuI">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuM">]</span></span></a></sup> <span about="#mwt770" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBuQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt770"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt770"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2025" about="#mwt770"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt770" id="mwBuU"/>, Japan has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_unemployment_rate" title="List of countries by unemployment rate" id="mwBuY">low unemployment rate</a> of around 2.5%.<sup about="#mwt778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-173" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-173"}}'><a href="#cite_note-173" id="mwBuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuk">[</span>172<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuo">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poverty_in_Japan" title="Poverty in Japan" id="mwBus">Its poverty rate</a> is the second highest among the G7 countries,<sup about="#mwt781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-174" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-174"}}'><a href="#cite_note-174" id="mwBuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBu0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu4">[</span>173<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu8">]</span></span></a></sup> and exceeds 15.7% of the population.<sup about="#mwt784" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-175" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175"}}'><a href="#cite_note-175" id="mwBvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvI">[</span>174<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvM">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan has the highest ratio of public debt to GDP among advanced economies,<sup about="#mwt787" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-176" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-176"}}'><a href="#cite_note-176" id="mwBvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvY">[</span>175<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvc">]</span></span></a></sup> with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_debt_of_Japan" title="National debt of Japan" id="mwBvg">a national debt</a> estimated at 237% relative to GDP <span about="#mwt771" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBvk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2026"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2026</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt771"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt771"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2026" about="#mwt771"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt771" id="mwBvo"/>.<sup about="#mwt790" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-177" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-177"}}'><a href="#cite_note-177" id="mwBvs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBv0">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBv4">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_yen" title="Japanese yen" id="mwBv8">Japanese yen</a> is the world's third-largest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reserve_currency" title="Reserve currency" id="mwBwA">reserve currency</a> after the US dollar and the euro.<sup about="#mwt793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-178" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-178"}}'><a href="#cite_note-178" id="mwBwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwM">[</span>177<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBwU">In 2024, Japan was the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_exports" title="List of countries by exports" id="mwBwY">eight-largest exporter</a><sup about="#mwt796" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-179" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-179"}}'><a href="#cite_note-179" id="mwBwc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwk">[</span>178<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwo">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_imports" title="List of countries by imports" id="mwBws">sixth-largest importer</a>.<sup about="#mwt799" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-180" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-180"}}'><a href="#cite_note-180" id="mwBww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBw0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBw4">[</span>179<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBw8">]</span></span></a></sup> Its exports amounted to 22.8% of its total GDP in 2024.<sup about="#mwt802" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-181" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181"}}'><a href="#cite_note-181" id="mwBxA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxI">[</span>180<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxM">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_the_largest_trading_partners_of_Japan" title="List of the largest trading partners of Japan" id="mwBxQ">Japan's main export markets</a> were China (22.8%, including Hong Kong) and the United States (18.5%).<sup about="#mwt805" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-STATJETRO_182-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"STATJETRO"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-STATJETRO-182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-STATJETRO-182" id="mwBxU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxc">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exports_of_Japan" title="List of exports of Japan" id="mwBxk">Its main exports</a> are motor vehicles, iron and steel products, semiconductors, and auto parts.<sup about="#mwt808" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-cia-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwBxo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxw">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBx0">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's main import markets in 2025 were China (23.8%) and the United States (11.4%).<sup about="#mwt809" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-STATJETRO_182-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"STATJETRO"}}'><a href="#cite_note-STATJETRO-182" id="mwBx4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBx8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByA">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByE">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's main imports are machinery and equipment, fossil fuels, foodstuffs, chemicals, and raw materials.<sup about="#mwt810" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-STATJETRO_182-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"STATJETRO"}}'><a href="#cite_note-STATJETRO-182" id="mwByI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwByM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByQ">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwByY">The Japanese variant of capitalism has many distinct features: <span title="Japanese-language romanization" about="#mwt811" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwByc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ja"},"2":{"wt":"[[keiretsu]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="ja-Latn"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keiretsu" title="Keiretsu">keiretsu</a></i></span> enterprises are influential, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lifetime_employment" title="Lifetime employment" class="mw-redirect" id="mwByg">lifetime employment</a> and seniority-based career advancement are common in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_work_environment" title="Japanese work environment" id="mwByk">Japanese work environment</a>.<sup about="#mwt815" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-oecd2008_183-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"oecd2008"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-oecd2008-183"}}'><a href="#cite_note-oecd2008-183" id="mwByo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBys"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByw">[</span>182<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt818" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-184" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-184"}}'><a href="#cite_note-184" id="mwBy4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBy8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzA">[</span>183<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzE">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan has a large <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooperative" title="Cooperative" id="mwBzI">cooperative</a> sector, with three of the world's ten largest cooperatives, including the largest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consumer_cooperative" title="Consumer cooperative" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBzM">consumer cooperative</a> and the largest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agricultural_cooperative" title="Agricultural cooperative" id="mwBzQ">agricultural cooperative</a> <span about="#mwt812" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBzU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt812"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt812"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2018" about="#mwt812"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt812" id="mwBzY"/>.<sup about="#mwt821" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-185" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-185"}}'><a href="#cite_note-185" id="mwBzc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzk">[</span>184<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzo">]</span></span></a></sup> It <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_rankings_of_Japan#Economy" title="International rankings of Japan" id="mwBzs">ranks highly</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Competition_(companies)" title="Competition (companies)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBzw">competitiveness</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economic_freedom" title="Economic freedom" id="mwBz0">economic freedom</a>. The country attracted 36.9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBz4"> </span>million international tourists in 2024,<sup about="#mwt824" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-186" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-186"}}'><a href="#cite_note-186" id="mwBz8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0E">[</span>185<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0I">]</span></span></a></sup> and was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Tourism_rankings" title="World Tourism rankings" id="mwB0M">ranked eleventh</a> in the world in 2019 for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inbound_tourism_(Japan)" title="Inbound tourism (Japan)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB0Q">inbound tourism</a>.<sup about="#mwt827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WTOB_187-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WTOB"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WTOB-187"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WTOB-187" id="mwB0U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0c">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0g">]</span></span></a></sup> The 2024 <i id="mwB0k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travel_and_Tourism_Competitiveness_Report" title="Travel and Tourism Competitiveness Report" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB0o">Travel and Tourism Competitiveness Report</a></i> ranked Japan third in the world.<sup about="#mwt830" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-188" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-188"}}'><a href="#cite_note-188" id="mwB0s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB00">[</span>187<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB04">]</span></span></a></sup> Its international tourism receipts in 2019 amounted to $46.1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB08"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt831" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WTOB_187-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WTOB"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WTOB-187" id="mwB1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1I">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1M">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwB1Q" aria-labelledby="Agriculture_and_fishery"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Agriculture_and_fishery">Agriculture and fishery</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt832" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB1U" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Agriculture, forestry, and fishing in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt833" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt832" id="mwB1Y">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agriculture,_forestry,_and_fishing_in_Japan" title="Agriculture, forestry, and fishing in Japan">Agriculture, forestry, and fishing in Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB1c"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu,_Japan.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB1g"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu,_Japan.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu%2C_Japan.JPG/250px-Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu%2C_Japan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu%2C_Japan.JPG/500px-Rice_Paddies_In_Aizu%2C_Japan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1600" data-file-height="1200" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB1k"/></a><figcaption id="mwB1o">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice_paddy" title="Rice paddy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB1s">rice paddy</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aizu" title="Aizu" id="mwB1w">Aizu</a>, Fukushima Prefecture</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB10">The Japanese agricultural sector accounts for about 1.2% of the country's total GDP <span about="#mwt834" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB14" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"lc":{"wt":"yes"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt834"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt834"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2018" about="#mwt834"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt834" id="mwB18"/>.<sup about="#mwt836" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sec_117-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sec"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sec-117" id="mwB2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2I">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2M">]</span></span></a></sup> Only 11.2% of Japan's land is suitable for cultivation.<sup about="#mwt839" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-189" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-189"}}'><a href="#cite_note-189" id="mwB2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2Y">[</span>188<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2c">]</span></span></a></sup> Because of this lack of arable land, a system of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrace_(earthworks)" title="Terrace (earthworks)" id="mwB2g">terraces</a> is used to farm in small areas.<sup about="#mwt842" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Urbanites_Help_Sustain_Japan's_Historic_Rice_Paddy_Terraces_190-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Urbanites Help Sustain Japan&apos;s Historic Rice Paddy Terraces"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Urbanites_Help_Sustain_Japan&apos;s_Historic_Rice_Paddy_Terraces-190"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Urbanites_Help_Sustain_Japan's_Historic_Rice_Paddy_Terraces-190" id="mwB2k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2s">[</span>189<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2w">]</span></span></a></sup> This results in one of the world's highest levels of crop yields per unit area, with an agricultural self-sufficiency rate of about 50% <span about="#mwt835" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB20" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2018</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt835"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt835"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2018" about="#mwt835"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt835" id="mwB24"/>.<sup about="#mwt845" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-191" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-191"}}'><a href="#cite_note-191" id="mwB28"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3E">[</span>190<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3I">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's small agricultural sector is highly subsidized and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agricultural_Protectionism_in_Japan" title="Agricultural Protectionism in Japan" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB3M">protected</a>.<sup about="#mwt848" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-192" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-192"}}'><a href="#cite_note-192" id="mwB3Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3Y">[</span>191<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3c">]</span></span></a></sup> There has been a growing concern about farming as farmers are aging with a difficult time finding successors.<sup about="#mwt851" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-193" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-193"}}'><a href="#cite_note-193" id="mwB3g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3o">[</span>192<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3s">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB3w">Japan ranked seventh in the world in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishing_industry_by_country" title="Fishing industry by country" id="mwB30">tonnage of fish caught</a> and captured 3,167,610 metric tons of fish in 2016, down from an annual average of 4,000,000 tons over the previous decade.<sup about="#mwt854" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-194" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-194"}}'><a href="#cite_note-194" id="mwB34"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB38"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4A">[</span>193<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4E">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan maintains one of the world's largest fishing fleets and accounts for nearly 15% of the global catch,<sup about="#mwt855" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwB4I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4Q">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4U">]</span></span></a></sup> prompting critiques that Japan's fishing is leading to depletion in fish stocks such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuna" title="Tuna" id="mwB4Y">tuna</a>.<sup about="#mwt858" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-195" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-195"}}'><a href="#cite_note-195" id="mwB4c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4k">[</span>194<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4o">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan has sparked controversy by supporting commercial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whaling_in_Japan" title="Whaling in Japan" id="mwB4s">whaling</a>.<sup about="#mwt861" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-196" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-196"}}'><a href="#cite_note-196" id="mwB4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB40"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB44">[</span>195<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB48">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwB5A" aria-labelledby="Industry_and_services"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Industry_and_services">Industry and services</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt862" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB5E" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Manufacturing in Japan"},"2":{"wt":"Trade and services in Japan"},"3":{"wt":"Electronics industry in Japan"},"4":{"wt":"Automotive industry in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt863" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt862" id="mwB5I">Main articles: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manufacturing_in_Japan" title="Manufacturing in Japan">Manufacturing in Japan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_and_services_in_Japan" title="Trade and services in Japan">Trade and services in Japan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronics_industry_in_Japan" title="Electronics industry in Japan">Electronics industry in Japan</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automotive_industry_in_Japan" title="Automotive industry in Japan">Automotive industry in Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB5M"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver,_Front_Right,_10-11-2022.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB5Q"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver,_Front_Right,_10-11-2022.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver%2C_Front_Right%2C_10-11-2022.jpg/250px-2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver%2C_Front_Right%2C_10-11-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver%2C_Front_Right%2C_10-11-2022.jpg/500px-2018_Nissan_GT-R_Premium_in_Super_Silver%2C_Front_Right%2C_10-11-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3423" data-file-height="1811" data-file-type="bitmap" height="132" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB5U"/></a><figcaption id="mwB5Y">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_GT-R" title="Nissan GT-R" id="mwB5c">Nissan GT-R</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sports_car" title="Sports car" id="mwB5g">sports car</a> manufactured by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan" title="Nissan" id="mwB5k">Nissan</a>. Japan is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_motor_vehicle_production" title="List of countries by motor vehicle production" id="mwB5o">third-largest producer of motor vehicles</a> in the world.<sup about="#mwt864" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_197-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-197" id="mwB5s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB50">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB54">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB58">Japan has a large industrial capacity and is home to some of the "largest and most technologically advanced producers of motor vehicles, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_tool" title="Machine tool" id="mwB6A">machine tools</a>, steel and nonferrous metals, ships, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_substance" title="Chemical substance" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB6E">chemical substances</a>, textiles, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Processed_foods" title="Processed foods" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB6I">processed foods</a>".<sup about="#mwt866" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwB6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6U">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6Y">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's industrial sector makes up approximately 27.5% of its GDP.<sup about="#mwt867" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwB6c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6k">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6o">]</span></span></a></sup> The country's manufacturing output is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_manufacturing_output" title="List of countries by manufacturing output" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB6s">third highest</a> in the world <span about="#mwt865" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB6w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2023"},"lc":{"wt":"yes"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2023</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt865"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt865"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2023" about="#mwt865"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt865" id="mwB60"/>.<sup about="#mwt870" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-198" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-198"}}'><a href="#cite_note-198" id="mwB64"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB68"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7A">[</span>197<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB7I">Japan is in the top three globally for both automobile production<sup about="#mwt873" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_197-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-197"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-197" id="mwB7M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7U">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7Y">]</span></span></a></sup> and export,<sup about="#mwt876" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-199" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-199"}}'><a href="#cite_note-199" id="mwB7c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7k">[</span>198<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt879" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-200" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-200"}}'><a href="#cite_note-200" id="mwB7s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB70">[</span>199<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB74">]</span></span></a></sup> and is home to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyota" title="Toyota" id="mwB78">Toyota</a>, the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_manufacturers_by_motor_vehicle_production" title="List of manufacturers by motor vehicle production" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB8A">largest automobile company by production</a>. The Japanese shipbuilding industry faces increasing competition from its East Asian neighbors, South Korea and China; a 2020 government initiative identified this sector as a target for increasing exports.<sup about="#mwt882" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-201" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-201"}}'><a href="#cite_note-201" id="mwB8E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8M">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB8U">Once considered the strongest in the world, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_consumer_electronics_industry" title="Japanese consumer electronics industry" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB8Y">Japanese consumer electronics industry</a> is in a state of decline as regional competition arises in neighboring East Asian countries such as South Korea and China.<sup about="#mwt885" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-202" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-202"}}'><a href="#cite_note-202" id="mwB8c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8k">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8o">]</span></span></a></sup> However, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_games_in_Japan" title="Video games in Japan" id="mwB8s">Japan's video game sector</a> remains a major industry; in 2014, Japan's consumer video game market grossed $9.6<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB8w"> </span>billion, with $5.8<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwB80"> </span>billion coming from mobile gaming.<sup about="#mwt888" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-203" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-203"}}'><a href="#cite_note-203" id="mwB84"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB88"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9A">[</span>202<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9E">]</span></span></a></sup> By 2015, Japan had become the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_video_games_markets_by_country" title="List of video games markets by country" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB9I">fourth-largest PC game</a> market by revenue, behind <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_games_in_China" title="Video games in China" id="mwB9M">China</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_games_in_the_United_States" title="Video games in the United States" id="mwB9Q">United States</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_games_in_South_Korea" title="Video games in South Korea" id="mwB9U">South Korea</a>.<sup about="#mwt891" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-204" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-204"}}'><a href="#cite_note-204" id="mwB9Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9g">[</span>203<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9k">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB9o">Japan's service sector accounts for about 69.8% of its total economic output <span about="#mwt892" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB9s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2023"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2023</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt892"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt892"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2023" about="#mwt892"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt892" id="mwB9w"/>.<sup about="#mwt895" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-205" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-205"}}'><a href="#cite_note-205" id="mwB90"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB94"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB98">[</span>204<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-A">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banking_in_Japan" title="Banking in Japan" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-E">Banking</a>, retail, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transportation_in_Japan" title="Transportation in Japan" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-I">transportation</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telecommunications_in_Japan" title="Telecommunications in Japan" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-M">telecommunications</a> are all major industries, with companies such as Toyota, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honda" title="Honda" id="mwB-Q">Honda</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yamaha_Motor_Company" title="Yamaha Motor Company" id="mwB-U">Yamaha</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitsubishi_UFJ" title="Mitsubishi UFJ" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-Y">Mitsubishi UFJ</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nippon_Telegraph_and_Telephone" title="Nippon Telegraph and Telephone" id="mwB-c">NTT</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeon_(company)" title="Aeon (company)" id="mwB-g">Aeon</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoftBank" title="SoftBank" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-k">SoftBank</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hitachi" title="Hitachi" id="mwB-o">Hitachi</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitsui" title="Mitsui" id="mwB-s">Mitsui</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itochu" title="Itochu" id="mwB-w">Itochu</a> listed as among the largest in the world.<sup about="#mwt898" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Fortune_Global_500_206-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Fortune Global 500"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Fortune_Global_500-206"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Fortune_Global_500-206" id="mwB-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-8">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt901" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-207" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-207"}}'><a href="#cite_note-207" id="mwB_E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_M">[</span>206<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwB_U" aria-labelledby="Science_and_technology"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Science_and_technology">Science and technology</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt902" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Science and technology in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt903" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt902" id="mwB_c">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_Japan" title="Science and technology in Japan">Science and technology in Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB_g"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB_k"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg/250px-Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg/500px-Kibo_PM_and_ELM-PS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3072" data-file-height="2039" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB_o"/></a><figcaption id="mwB_s">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Experiment_Module" title="Japanese Experiment Module" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB_w">Japanese Experiment Module</a> (<span title="Japanese-language romanization" about="#mwt904" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB_0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ja"},"2":{"wt":"Kibō"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="ja-Latn">Kibō</i></span>) at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Space_Station" title="International Space Station" id="mwB_4">International Space Station</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwB_8">Relative to gross domestic product, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Research_and_development_in_Japan" title="Research and development in Japan" id="mwCAA">Japan's research and development</a> budget is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sovereign_states_by_research_and_development_spending" title="List of sovereign states by research and development spending" id="mwCAE">sixth or seventh highest</a> in the world,<sup about="#mwt908" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-208" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-208"}}'><a href="#cite_note-208" id="mwCAI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAQ">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAU">]</span></span></a></sup> with 907,400 researchers sharing a 22-trillion-yen research and development budget <span about="#mwt905" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCAY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2023"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2023</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt905"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt905"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2023" about="#mwt905"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt905" id="mwCAc"/>.<sup about="#mwt911" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-209" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-209"}}'><a href="#cite_note-209" id="mwCAg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAo">[</span>208<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAs">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan has the second highest number of researchers in science and technology per capita in the world with 14 per 1000 employees.<sup about="#mwt914" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-210" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-210"}}'><a href="#cite_note-210" id="mwCAw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCA0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA4">[</span>209<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA8">]</span></span></a></sup> The country has produced twenty-two <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobel_Prize" title="Nobel Prize" id="mwCBA">Nobel laureates</a> in either physics, chemistry or medicine,<sup about="#mwt917" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-211" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-211"}}'><a href="#cite_note-211" id="mwCBE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBM">[</span>210<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and three <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fields_Medal" title="Fields Medal" id="mwCBU">Fields medalists</a>.<sup about="#mwt920" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-212" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-212"}}'><a href="#cite_note-212" id="mwCBY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBg">[</span>211<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCBo">Japan is a leading <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_robotics" title="Japanese robotics" id="mwCBs">robotics</a> producer, supplying 38% of the world's 2024 total,<sup about="#mwt923" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-213" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-213"}}'><a href="#cite_note-213" id="mwCBw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCB0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB4">[</span>212<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB8">]</span></span></a></sup> down from 55% in 2017.<sup about="#mwt926" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-214" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-214"}}'><a href="#cite_note-214" id="mwCCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCI">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCCQ">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Aerospace_Exploration_Agency" title="Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCCU">Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency</a> is Japan's national <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_agency" title="Space agency" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCCY">space agency</a>; it conducts space, planetary, and aviation research, and leads development of rockets and satellites.<sup about="#mwt930" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-215" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-215"}}'><a href="#cite_note-215" id="mwCCc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCk">[</span>214<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCo">]</span></span></a></sup> It is a participant in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Space_Station" title="International Space Station" id="mwCCs">International Space Station</a>: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Experiment_Module" title="Japanese Experiment Module" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCCw">Japanese Experiment Module</a> (<span title="Japanese-language romanization" about="#mwt927" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCC0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ja"},"2":{"wt":"Kibō"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="ja-Latn">Kibō</i></span>) was added to the station during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle" title="Space Shuttle" id="mwCC4">Space Shuttle</a> assembly flights in 2008.<sup about="#mwt933" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-216" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-216"}}'><a href="#cite_note-216" id="mwCC8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDE">[</span>215<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDI">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_probe" title="Space probe" id="mwCDM">space probe</a> <i id="mwCDQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akatsuki_(spacecraft)" title="Akatsuki (spacecraft)" id="mwCDU">Akatsuki</a></i> was launched in 2010 and achieved orbit around Venus in 2015.<sup about="#mwt936" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-217" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-217" id="mwCDY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDg">[</span>216<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDk">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's plans in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_exploration" title="Space exploration" id="mwCDo">space exploration</a> include building a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonization_of_the_Moon" title="Colonization of the Moon" id="mwCDs">Moon base</a> and landing astronauts by 2030.<sup about="#mwt939" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-218" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-218"}}'><a href="#cite_note-218" id="mwCDw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCD0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCD4">[</span>217<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCD8">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2007, it launched lunar explorer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SELENE" title="SELENE" id="mwCEA">SELENE</a> (Selenological and Engineering Explorer) from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanegashima_Space_Center" title="Tanegashima Space Center" id="mwCEE">Tanegashima Space Center</a>. The largest lunar mission since the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_program" title="Apollo program" id="mwCEI">Apollo program</a>, its purpose was to gather data on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon#Formation" title="Moon" id="mwCEM">Moon's origin and evolution</a>. The explorer entered a lunar orbit on October 4, 2007,<sup about="#mwt942" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-219" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-219"}}'><a href="#cite_note-219" id="mwCEQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEY">[</span>218<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt945" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-220" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-220"}}'><a href="#cite_note-220" id="mwCEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEo">[</span>219<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEs">]</span></span></a></sup> and was deliberately crashed into the Moon on June 11, 2009.<sup about="#mwt948" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-221" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-221"}}'><a href="#cite_note-221" id="mwCEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE4">[</span>220<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwCFA" aria-labelledby="Infrastructure"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Infrastructure">Infrastructure</h2></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwCFE" aria-labelledby="Transportation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Transportation">Transportation</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt949" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCFI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Transport in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt950" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt949" id="mwCFM">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport_in_Japan" title="Transport in Japan">Transport in Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCFQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Japan_Airlines,_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_(19455285040).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCFU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Japan_Airlines,_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_(19455285040).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Japan_Airlines%2C_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_%2819455285040%29.jpg/250px-Japan_Airlines%2C_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_%2819455285040%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Japan_Airlines%2C_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_%2819455285040%29.jpg/500px-Japan_Airlines%2C_Boeing_787-9_JA861J_NRT_%2819455285040%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4678" data-file-height="3120" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCFY"/></a><figcaption id="mwCFc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Airlines" title="Japan Airlines" id="mwCFg">Japan Airlines</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_carrier" title="Flag carrier" id="mwCFk">flag carrier</a> of Japan</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCFo">Japan has invested heavily in transportation infrastructure since the 1990s.<sup about="#mwt959" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-222" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-222"}}'><a href="#cite_note-222" id="mwCFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF0">[</span>221<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF4">]</span></span></a></sup> The country has approximately <span about="#mwt951" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCF8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"comma":{"wt":"5"},"1":{"wt":"1200000"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"},"sp":{"wt":"us"}},"i":0}}]}'>1,200,000 kilometers (750,000 miles)</span> of roads made up of <span about="#mwt952" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCGA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"comma":{"wt":"5"},"1":{"wt":"1000000"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"},"sp":{"wt":"us"}},"i":0}}]}'>1,000,000 kilometers (620,000 miles)</span> of city, town, and village roads, <span about="#mwt953" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCGE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"comma":{"wt":"5"},"1":{"wt":"130000"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"},"sp":{"wt":"us"}},"i":0}}]}'>130,000 kilometers (81,000 miles)</span> of prefectural roads, <span about="#mwt954" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCGI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"comma":{"wt":"5"},"1":{"wt":"54736"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"},"sp":{"wt":"us"}},"i":0}}]}'>54,736 kilometers (34,011 miles)</span> of general national highways, and <span about="#mwt955" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCGM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"comma":{"wt":"5"},"1":{"wt":"7641"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"},"sp":{"wt":"us"}},"i":0}}]}'>7641 kilometers (4748 miles)</span> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expressways_of_Japan" title="Expressways of Japan" id="mwCGQ">national expressways</a> <span about="#mwt956" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCGU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2017"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2017</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt956"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt956"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2017" about="#mwt956"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt956" id="mwCGY"/>.<sup about="#mwt962" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-223" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-223"}}'><a href="#cite_note-223" id="mwCGc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGk">[</span>222<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCGs">Since privatization in 1987,<sup about="#mwt965" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-224" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-224"}}'><a href="#cite_note-224" id="mwCGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCG0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCG4">[</span>223<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCG8">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_railway_companies_in_Japan" title="List of railway companies in Japan" id="mwCHA">dozens of Japanese railway companies</a> compete in regional and local passenger transportation markets; major companies include seven <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Railways_Group" title="Japan Railways Group" id="mwCHE">JR</a> enterprises, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kintetsu_Railway" title="Kintetsu Railway" id="mwCHI">Kintetsu</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seibu_Railway" title="Seibu Railway" id="mwCHM">Seibu Railway</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keio_Corporation" title="Keio Corporation" id="mwCHQ">Keio Corporation</a>. The high-speed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinkansen" title="Shinkansen" id="mwCHU">Shinkansen</a> (bullet trains) that connect major cities are known for their safety and punctuality.<sup about="#mwt968" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-225" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-225"}}'><a href="#cite_note-225" id="mwCHY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHg">[</span>224<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCHo">There are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_airports_in_Japan" title="List of airports in Japan" id="mwCHs">280 airports in Japan</a> <span about="#mwt969" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCHw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt969"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt969"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2025" about="#mwt969"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt969" id="mwCH0"/>.<sup about="#mwt971" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cia_85-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cia-85" id="mwCH4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCH8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIA">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIE">]</span></span></a></sup> The largest domestic airport, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haneda_Airport" title="Haneda Airport" id="mwCII">Haneda Airport</a> in Tokyo, was Asia's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_busiest_airports_by_passenger_traffic" title="List of busiest airports by passenger traffic" id="mwCIM">second-busiest airport</a> in 2019.<sup about="#mwt974" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-226" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-226"}}'><a href="#cite_note-226" id="mwCIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIY">[</span>225<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIc">]</span></span></a></sup> The Keihin and Hanshin superport hubs are among the largest in the world, at 7.98 and 5.22<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCIg"> </span>million <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twenty-foot_equivalent_unit" title="Twenty-foot equivalent unit" id="mwCIk">TEU</a> respectively <span about="#mwt970" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCIo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2017"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of 2017</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt970"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt970"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2017" about="#mwt970"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt970" id="mwCIs"/>.<sup about="#mwt977" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-227" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-227"}}'><a href="#cite_note-227" id="mwCIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI4">[</span>226<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwCJA" aria-labelledby="Energy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Energy">Energy</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt978" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCJE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Energy in Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt979" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt978" id="mwCJI">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy_in_Japan" title="Energy in Japan">Energy in Japan</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCJM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCJQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg/250px-Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg/500px-Wind_turbines_lined_up_along_the_coast_of_Katagami_City_20221025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="3375" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCJU"/></a><figcaption id="mwCJY">Wind turbines at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katagami,_Akita" title="Katagami, Akita" id="mwCJc">Katagami</a>, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akita_Prefecture" title="Akita Prefecture" id="mwCJg">Akita Prefecture</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCJk"><span about="#mwt980" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCJo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2019"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2019</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt980"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt980"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2019" about="#mwt980"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt980" id="mwCJs"/>, 37.1% of energy in Japan is produced from petroleum, 25.1% from coal, 22.4% from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_gas" title="Natural gas" id="mwCJw">natural gas</a>, 3.5% from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydropower" title="Hydropower" id="mwCJ0">hydropower</a> and 2.8% from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_power_in_Japan" title="Nuclear power in Japan" id="mwCJ4">nuclear power</a>, among other sources. Nuclear power was down from 11.2% in 2010.<sup about="#mwt983" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-228" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-228"}}'><a href="#cite_note-228" id="mwCJ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKE">[</span>227<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKI">]</span></span></a></sup> By May 2012 all of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nuclear_power_plants_in_Japan" title="List of nuclear power plants in Japan" id="mwCKM">the country's nuclear power plants</a> had been taken offline because of ongoing public opposition following the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fukushima_nuclear_accident" title="Fukushima nuclear accident" id="mwCKQ">Fukushima nuclear accident</a> in March 2011, though government officials continued to try to sway public opinion in favor of returning at least some to service.<sup about="#mwt986" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-229" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-229"}}'><a href="#cite_note-229" id="mwCKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKc">[</span>228<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKg">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sendai_Nuclear_Power_Plant" title="Sendai Nuclear Power Plant" id="mwCKk">Sendai Nuclear Power Plant</a> restarted in 2015,<sup about="#mwt989" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-230" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-230"}}'><a href="#cite_note-230" id="mwCKo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKw">[</span>229<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCK0">]</span></span></a></sup> and since then several other nuclear power plants have been restarted.<sup about="#mwt992" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-231" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-231"}}'><a href="#cite_note-231" id="mwCK4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCK8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLA">[</span>230<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLE">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan lacks significant domestic reserves and has a heavy dependence on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_oil_imports" title="List of countries by oil imports" id="mwCLI">imported energy</a>.<sup about="#mwt995" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-232" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-232"}}'><a href="#cite_note-232" id="mwCLM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLU">[</span>231<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLY">]</span></span></a></sup> The country has therefore aimed to diversify its sources and maintain high levels of energy efficiency.<sup about="#mwt998" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-233" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-233"}}'><a href="#cite_note-233" id="mwCLc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLk">[</span>232<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwCLs" aria-labelledby="Demographics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Demographics">Demographics</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt999" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCLw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Demographics of Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1000" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt999" id="mwCL0">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_Japan" title="Demographics of Japan">Demographics of Japan</a></div>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1001" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCL4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Japanese people"},"2":{"wt":"Ethnic groups of Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1002" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1001" id="mwCL8">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_people" title="Japanese people">Japanese people</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethnic_groups_of_Japan" title="Ethnic groups of Japan">Ethnic groups of Japan</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCMA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCME"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG/330px-Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG/960px-Tokyo_from_the_top_of_the_SkyTree.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5999" data-file-height="3598" data-file-type="bitmap" height="180" width="300" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1.2" id="mwCMI"/></a><figcaption id="mwCMM">View of Tokyo from the top of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Skytree" title="Tokyo Skytree" id="mwCMQ">Tokyo Skytree</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Tokyo_Area" title="Greater Tokyo Area" id="mwCMU">Greater Tokyo Area</a> is ranked as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_metropolitan_areas_by_population" title="List of metropolitan areas by population" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCMY">most populous metropolitan area</a> in the world.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCMc">Japan has a population of nearly 123<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCMg"> </span>million, of whom almost 119<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCMk"> </span>million are Japanese nationals; foreign residents make up the remainder, estimated at 3,743,000 as of September 2025.<sup about="#mwt1005" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-234" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-234"}}'><a href="#cite_note-234" id="mwCMo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMw">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCM0">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan is one of the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aging_of_Japan" title="Aging of Japan" id="mwCM4">fastest aging countries</a> and has the highest proportion of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elderly_people_in_Japan" title="Elderly people in Japan" id="mwCM8">elderly citizens</a> of any country, comprising <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_age_structure" title="List of countries by age structure" id="mwCNA">one-third of its total population</a>;<sup about="#mwt1008" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EUAgeing_235-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EUAgeing"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EUAgeing-235"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EUAgeing-235" id="mwCNE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNM">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNQ">]</span></span></a></sup> this is the result of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post–World_War_II_baby_boom" title="Post–World War II baby boom" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCNU">post–World War II baby boom</a>, which was followed by an increase in life expectancy and a decrease in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birth_rate" title="Birth rate" id="mwCNY">birth rates</a>.<sup about="#mwt1011" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-236" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-236"}}'><a href="#cite_note-236" id="mwCNc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNk">[</span>235<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCNs">Japan has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_fertility_rate" title="Total fertility rate" id="mwCNw">total fertility rate</a> of 1.2, which is below the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-replacement_fertility" title="Sub-replacement fertility" id="mwCN0">replacement rate</a> of 2.1, and is among <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_total_fertility_rate" title="List of countries by total fertility rate" id="mwCN4">the world's lowest</a>:<sup about="#mwt1015" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-237" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-237"}}'><a href="#cite_note-237" id="mwCN8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOE">[</span>236<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOI">]</span></span></a></sup> it has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Median_age" title="Median age" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOM">median age</a> of 48.4, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_median_age" title="List of countries by median age" id="mwCOQ">highest in the world</a>.<sup about="#mwt1018" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IMFAgeing_238-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IMFAgeing"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IMFAgeing-238"}}'><a href="#cite_note-IMFAgeing-238" id="mwCOU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOc">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOg">]</span></span></a></sup> <span about="#mwt1012" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCOk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt1012"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Japan&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt1012"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2025" about="#mwt1012"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt1012" id="mwCOo"/>, over 29.3% of the population is over 65, or more than one in four out of the Japanese population.<sup about="#mwt1021" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-November_2020_population_estimate_239-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"November 2020 population estimate"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-November_2020_population_estimate-239"}}'><a href="#cite_note-November_2020_population_estimate-239" id="mwCOs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO0">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO4">]</span></span></a></sup> As a growing number of younger Japanese are not marrying or remaining childless,<sup about="#mwt1024" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Walia_240-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Walia"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Walia-240"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Walia-240" id="mwCO8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPE">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1027" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241"}}'><a href="#cite_note-241" id="mwCPM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPU">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPY">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan's population is expected to drop to around 88<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCPc"> </span>million by 2065.<sup about="#mwt1028" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EUAgeing_235-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EUAgeing"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EUAgeing-235" id="mwCPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPo">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCPw">The changes in demographic structure have created several social issues, particularly a decline in the workforce population and an increase in the cost of social security benefits.<sup about="#mwt1029" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Walia_240-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Walia"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Walia-240" id="mwCP0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCP4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCP8">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQA">]</span></span></a></sup> The Government of Japan projects that there will be almost one elderly person for each person of working age by 2060.<sup about="#mwt1030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IMFAgeing_238-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IMFAgeing"}}'><a href="#cite_note-IMFAgeing-238" id="mwCQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQM">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immigration_to_Japan" title="Immigration to Japan" id="mwCQU">Immigration</a> and birth incentives are sometimes suggested as a solution to provide younger workers to support the nation's aging population.<sup about="#mwt1033" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-242" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-242"}}'><a href="#cite_note-242" id="mwCQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQg">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1036" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-243" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-243" id="mwCQo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQw">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQ0">]</span></span></a></sup> On April 1, 2019, Japan enacted its revised immigration law, protecting the rights of foreign workers to help reduce labor shortages in certain sectors.<sup about="#mwt1039" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-244" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244"}}'><a href="#cite_note-244" id="mwCQ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRA">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCRI">In 2023, 92% of the Japanese population lived in cities.<sup about="#mwt1043" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-245" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-245" id="mwCRM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRU">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRY">]</span></span></a></sup> The capital city, Tokyo, has a population of 13.9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCRc"> </span>million (2022).<sup about="#mwt1046" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-toukei-metro_246-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"toukei-metro"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-toukei-metro-246"}}'><a href="#cite_note-toukei-metro-246" id="mwCRg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRo">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRs">]</span></span></a></sup> It is part of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Tokyo_Area" title="Greater Tokyo Area" id="mwCRw">Greater Tokyo Area</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_metropolitan_areas_by_population" title="List of metropolitan areas by population" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCR0">biggest metropolitan area</a> in the world with 37.4<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCR4"> </span>million people (2024).<sup about="#mwt1049" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwCR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSE">[</span>246<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSI">]</span></span></a></sup> Japan is an ethnically and culturally <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_ranked_by_ethnic_and_cultural_diversity_level" title="List of countries ranked by ethnic and cultural diversity level" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCSM">homogeneous society</a>,<sup about="#mwt1052" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-248" id="mwCSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSY">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSc">]</span></span></a></sup> with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_people" title="Japanese people" id="mwCSg">Japanese people</a> forming 97.4% of the country's population.<sup about="#mwt1055" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-249" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-249" id="mwCSk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSs">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSw">]</span></span></a></sup> Minority ethnic groups in the country include the indigenous <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ainu_people" title="Ainu people" id="mwCS0">Ainu</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryukyuan_people" title="Ryukyuan people" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCS4">Ryukyuan people</a>.<sup about="#mwt1058" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-250" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-250"}}'><a href="#cite_note-250" id="mwCS8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTE">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTI">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zainichi_Koreans" title="Zainichi Koreans" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCTM">Zainichi Koreans</a>,<sup about="#mwt1061" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-251" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-251"}}'><a href="#cite_note-251" id="mwCTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTY">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTc">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_people_in_Japan" title="Chinese people in Japan" id="mwCTg">Chinese</a>,<sup about="#mwt1064" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-252" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-252"}}'><a href="#cite_note-252" id="mwCTk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTs">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filipinos_in_Japan" title="Filipinos in Japan" id="mwCT0">Filipinos</a>,<sup about="#mwt1067" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-253" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-253"}}'><a href="#cite_note-253" id="mwCT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUA">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUE">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Brazilian" title="Japanese Brazilian" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCUI">Brazilians mostly of Japanese descent</a>,<sup about="#mwt1070" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-254" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-254"}}'><a href="#cite_note-254" id="mwCUM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCUQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUU">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUY">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Peruvian" title="Japanese Peruvian" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCUc">Peruvians mostly of Japanese descent</a> are also among Japan's small minority groups.<sup about="#mwt1073" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-255" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-255"}}'><a href="#cite_note-255" id="mwCUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCUk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUo">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUs">]</span></span></a></sup> <span title="Japanese-language romanization" about="#mwt1040" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCUw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ja"},"2":{"wt":"[[Burakumin]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="ja-Latn"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burakumin" title="Burakumin">Burakumin</a></i></span> make up a social minority group.<sup about="#mwt1076" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-256" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256"}}'><a href="#cite_note-256" id="mwCU0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCU4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCU8">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

